@startuml undo-redo
|User|
start
if (Kind of change?) then (visual edit or project operation)
  |Editor|
  :Record one history entry, including any linked
  changes (link updates, lane moves, re-division);
elseif (Kind of change?) then (typing in a property field)
  |Editor|
  :Record one entry when the field loses
  focus or the user presses Enter;
else (typing in the source)
  |Editor|
  :Group the typing into one entry, ending when
  the user pauses or leaves the source view;
endif
|User|
:Choose Undo or Redo, which names the action;
|Editor|
if (Typing in progress in a focused text field?) then (yes)
  :Undo typing within that field first;
else (no)
  :Open the affected screen or flow;
  :Restore its structure, properties and source together;
  :Select the affected element and announce what changed;
  if (Restored source valid?) then (yes)
    :The canvas is editable;
  else (no)
    :Show the block as invalid: last working
    version, read-only, with the problem;
  endif
endif
|User|
stop
@enduml
